  "scope": [
    "Retain original task grants and bind descendants from canonical SDK parent/child notifications. Ordinary SDK model headers, registered host tools, command deadline lookup and events use the retained owner.",
    "Per-task model counters reserve before awaits and share the unchanged 200-request process ceiling; model forwarding is bounded by its own grant deadline.",
    "Canonical returned SDK turn records protect delayed creation notifications from a newer foreground context; unknown session tags wait at most one second and never adopt the current grant.",
    "Keep the official DeepSeekSearchProvider and its result mapping, token/use limits and cancellation; replace its untagged internal route with an initiating-session route and charge auxiliary requests to the same retained grant.",
    "Live earlier child questions remain answerable in their own turn, carry a short earlier-task label and close at their original deadline. Workspace cancellation revokes all retained grants.",
    "The required command-deadline test keeps both artifact invariants, requests a 30-second foreground wait within the separate 20-second task budget, and records tools/jobs on failure."
  ],
  "boundaries": [
    "Direct SDK probes intentionally bypass only the outer isolation launcher through archived test-only loaders. They are not native application isolation acceptance.",
    "All provider responses and search sources are synthetic loopback fixtures. No external model or web search was called; there is no reasoning benchmark score.",
    "Root-session automatic wakeups still use the current root context. This iteration proves descendant ownership, not complete causal isolation of all parent wakeups.",
    "Legacy requests without a session tag retain current-context handling. Normal SDK calls and the configured official search adapter are tagged; arbitrary future providers require their own integration.",
    "Retain at most 256 grants and 4096 session/turn mappings; evicted or unknown descendants fail closed rather than adopting another task.",
    "The initial command-deadline Windows run failed; see ../command-deadline/windows-initial-failure.json. Its underlying cause was not established from the available tool trace, and the revised source/packaged test remains pending CI.",
    "Two new broker test fixtures initially sent string chunks to Buffer.concat and returned 400; they were corrected to Buffer chunks. The failed fixture log is retained separately and is not counted as a product failure or a pass.",
    "The full browser suite and Linux isolated SDK suite were not rerun. Native GUI checks use explicitly labeled host snapshots."
  ],
  "replay": {
    "instructions": "Copy probe files together into a fresh directory under .runtime (two levels below the repository root) and use the pinned Node runtime. child-owner-probe.mjs runs control or --followup; advisory/deadline/answer probes use --followup --funded; search probe uses --followup with or without --funded. Each case should use its own fresh directory to retain raw events. Baseline source is source_parent_commit; current replay uses current source.",
    "probe_directory": "probe/"
  },
